1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:03,101
Laos, spring 1975.

2
00:00:03,171 --> 00:00:08,320
Saigon has fallen, the Americans are leaving, and the people who
fought beside them have nowhere to go.

3
00:00:08,390 --> 00:00:14,143
This is Chao Fa, a cooperative board game based on real-life stories,
and this video will teach you how to play it.

4
00:00:15,063 --> 00:00:26,133
We will look at the goal of the game, the pieces in the box, how to set it up,
what a season of play looks like, the actions, fights, the story cloth, Winter,
the river crossing, and how the game ends.

5
00:00:26,203 --> 00:00:28,323
Then we will play through a season together.

6
00:00:28,393 --> 00:00:31,371
The chapter markers on screen let you jump to any part.

7
00:00:35,491 --> 00:00:36,647
You are Hmong.

8
00:00:36,717 --> 00:00:43,515
You are a countryless nation: a people with no country of your own,
and after this spring, not even the hills you were born in.

9
00:00:43,585 --> 00:00:47,747
Your village secretly supported the United States and its CIA-backed
army.

10
00:00:47,817 --> 00:00:51,922
Now the communists hold the capital, and the family must flee into the
jungle.

11
00:00:52,842 --> 00:00:55,402
The goal is simple to say and hard to do.

12
00:00:55,472 --> 00:00:58,613
Walk south through the hills, the jungle and the lowlands.

13
00:00:58,683 --> 00:01:04,576
Recover the nine squares of a story cloth, each one won with a key: a
contact, a route, a signal.

14
00:01:04,646 --> 00:01:06,986
Then cross the Mekong River into Thailand.

15
00:01:07,056 --> 00:01:13,528
You have five years: twenty seasons, from spring 1975 to the winter of
1979.

16
00:01:14,448 --> 00:01:20,190
Chao Fa is fully cooperative, for one to six players, and a game takes
ninety minutes to three hours.

17
00:01:20,260 --> 00:01:23,482
Everyone at the table plays one villager of the same family.

18
00:01:23,552 --> 00:01:29,154
You win together when at least one person reaches the Thai bank, and
you lose together when no one does.

19
00:01:29,224 --> 00:01:31,041
It is a hard game by design.

20
00:01:31,111 --> 00:01:35,332
Play it like the people it is about: carefully, together, and without
giving up.

21
00:01:39,452 --> 00:01:40,898
Let's look at what you play with.

22
00:01:40,968 --> 00:01:45,850
Sixteen villager cards: nine men and boys, seven women and girls.

23
00:01:45,920 --> 00:01:47,366
Each has three numbers.

24
00:01:47,436 --> 00:01:53,642
HP is how many wounds they can take, ATK is what they add to the
family's attack, and DEF to its defence.

25
00:01:53,712 --> 00:01:57,062
Every villager has six points in all, divided differently.

26
00:01:57,132 --> 00:01:59,646
Side A gives a power used once a season.

27
00:01:59,716 --> 00:02:02,230
Side B gives a trait that is always on.

28
00:02:02,300 --> 00:02:05,139
You pick a side at setup and keep it for the whole game.

29
00:02:06,059 --> 00:02:13,623
Sixteen place tiles make the map: the home village, then four rows of
three places, the hills, the jungle, the lowlands and the river.

30
00:02:13,693 --> 00:02:19,493
Each tile shows its danger number, the grade of fight you meet there,
and what can be foraged in each season.

31
00:02:19,563 --> 00:02:28,451
Every place has its own search deck, with that place's picture on the back: the
items, food, shelter, clues, keys and dangers you would really find there.

32
00:02:29,371 --> 00:02:30,724
Then the shared decks.

33
00:02:30,794 --> 00:02:37,592
Eighty-five Season cards: patrols, ambushes, fog, food, omens, history
and moral dilemmas.

34
00:02:37,662 --> 00:02:40,292
One is drawn at the start of every season.

35
00:02:40,362 --> 00:02:44,316
Stranger cards, people you meet on the trail, each a choice of two.

36
00:02:44,386 --> 00:02:49,500
Six Turning Point cards, six Law cards, and twenty-one River cards for
the crossing.

37
00:02:50,420 --> 00:02:51,587
And the Fortune deck.

38
00:02:51,657 --> 00:02:53,800
Twenty cards numbered one to twenty.

39
00:02:53,870 --> 00:02:55,478
There are no dice in Chao Fa.

40
00:02:55,548 --> 00:02:59,327
Whenever the game needs a number, you draw the top card of the Fortune
deck.

41
00:02:59,397 --> 00:03:00,774
We will come back to it.

42
00:03:01,694 --> 00:03:09,316
The board holds the map and its search decks on the left, and on the
right the time track, Food, Hope, the story cloth and the phase track.

43
00:03:09,386 --> 00:03:11,993
Along the bottom runs the Mekong crossing lane.

44
00:03:12,063 --> 00:03:22,669
There is a standee for every villager, a party pawn, tokens and markers, a fight
tracker, the two-faced Patrol table card, a family board for every seat, and the
nine squares of the story cloth.

45
00:03:26,789 --> 00:03:27,666
Setting up.

46
00:03:27,736 --> 00:03:31,910
Put the Village Ruins at the top of the map, face up, and the party
pawn on it.

47
00:03:31,980 --> 00:03:38,801
For each row below it, shuffle that row's four tiles, lay three of
them face down, and put the fourth back in the box.

48
00:03:38,871 --> 00:03:41,188
The river row has only three tiles.

49
00:03:41,258 --> 00:03:44,666
Shuffle each place's search deck and set it beside its tile.

50
00:03:44,736 --> 00:03:48,631
Or use a setup card, which lays the tiles in a historical order.

51
00:03:49,551 --> 00:03:50,753
Now the family.

52
00:03:50,823 --> 00:03:53,395
The party is always three to six villagers.

53
00:03:53,465 --> 00:03:58,835
One player runs three, two players run two each, and three to six
players take one each.

54
00:03:58,905 --> 00:04:01,024
Each player chooses side A or B.

55
00:04:01,094 --> 00:04:06,627
Every villager starts with one item: the first of their own items, the
one thing they carried out of the village.

56
00:04:06,697 --> 00:04:09,896
Take it out of its search deck and put it on the family board.

57
00:04:09,966 --> 00:04:12,990
A good first party is Chai, Mai, Chao and Blong.

58
00:04:13,910 --> 00:04:18,874
Set Food to three times the number of villagers: a party of four
starts with twelve.

59
00:04:18,944 --> 00:04:24,116
Set Hope to three, and the time marker on season one, Spring 1975.

60
00:04:24,186 --> 00:04:35,849
A small family starts with the first squares of the cloth already sewn: a party
of six starts with squares one and two, five with one to three, four with one to
four, and three with one to five.

61
00:04:35,919 --> 00:04:37,249
The rest you must win.

62
00:04:38,169 --> 00:04:39,673
Shuffle the Fortune deck.

63
00:04:39,743 --> 00:04:47,551
Shuffle the Season deck in two stacks: the cards marked From 1977 go
under the rest, so the war arrives in its own time.

64
00:04:47,621 --> 00:04:53,641
Shuffle the Laws, the Strangers, the Turning Points and the River
deck, and set its three monsoon cards aside.

65
00:04:53,711 --> 00:04:56,492
Keep the Ending and Voice cards for the end of the game.

66
00:04:56,562 --> 00:04:57,729
You are ready to play.

67
00:05:01,849 --> 00:05:07,335
A game is up to twenty seasons, and one season is one round of the
table, in three steps.

68
00:05:07,405 --> 00:05:10,116
First, draw a Season card and resolve it.

69
00:05:10,186 --> 00:05:12,840
Second, each villager takes two actions.

70
00:05:12,910 --> 00:05:20,010
Third, the end of the season: sick people nobody nursed draw for
fever, and in Winter everyone eats and faces the Toll.

71
00:05:20,080 --> 00:05:22,524
Then the time marker moves forward one season.

72
00:05:22,594 --> 00:05:24,225
Time only moves forward.

73
00:05:25,145 --> 00:05:26,672
The Season card first.

74
00:05:26,742 --> 00:05:29,349
A patrol card is a fight wherever you are.

75
00:05:29,419 --> 00:05:30,830
Food goes to the store.

76
00:05:30,900 --> 00:05:34,470
A fog or shelter card goes to a player's hand to use later.

77
00:05:34,540 --> 00:05:36,451
A Time card costs you time.

78
00:05:36,521 --> 00:05:43,516
A dilemma must be answered by the whole party before anyone acts, and
an omen stays face up, moving you toward the Turning Point.

79
00:05:44,436 --> 00:05:45,673
Then the actions.

80
00:05:45,743 --> 00:05:48,559
Each villager takes two, or one if they are sick.

81
00:05:48,629 --> 00:05:51,711
If Hope is at zero, everyone has one action less.

82
00:05:51,781 --> 00:05:56,246
Go around the table; a villager may take both actions at once or split
them.

83
00:05:56,316 --> 00:06:02,197
Travel is the exception: the whole party moves together, and only
before anyone has acted that season.

84
00:06:03,117 --> 00:06:06,223
One rule shapes the whole game: hard work eats.

85
00:06:06,293 --> 00:06:11,663
A Search, a Scout, building a camp, and a journey each cost one Food
from the store.

86
00:06:11,733 --> 00:06:15,222
With no Food left, the worker still goes, but takes a wound.

87
00:06:15,292 --> 00:06:17,992
Outside Winter, nobody eats at the end of the season.

88
00:06:18,062 --> 00:06:21,423
You eat by working, so every action is a choice about food.

89
00:06:25,543 --> 00:06:26,478
The actions.

90
00:06:26,548 --> 00:06:28,319
Search is the heart of the game.

91
00:06:28,389 --> 00:06:31,925
Pay one Food and draw the top card of this place's search deck.

92
00:06:31,995 --> 00:06:35,936
An item goes to anyone in the party; a villager's own item goes to
them.

93
00:06:36,006 --> 00:06:37,336
Food goes to the store.

94
00:06:37,406 --> 00:06:40,025
Shelter and remedy cards go to your hand.

95
00:06:40,095 --> 00:06:42,551
A Danger card is a fight, right now.

96
00:06:42,621 --> 00:06:44,589
A key starts a key encounter.

97
00:06:45,509 --> 00:06:47,860
Searching the same place again makes noise.

98
00:06:47,930 --> 00:06:55,657
Before the second and every later search, draw a Fortune card: on the
number of earlier searches here or less, soldiers come to look.

99
00:06:55,727 --> 00:06:59,367
You fight at the place's level, with no spoils, and then you search.

100
00:06:59,437 --> 00:07:03,333
Cover your tracks once a season, and the place counts two fewer
searches.

101
00:07:04,253 --> 00:07:05,838
Scout, one Food.

102
00:07:05,908 --> 00:07:11,603
Turn face up one hidden tile next to the party: ahead, diagonally
ahead, or to the side.

103
00:07:11,673 --> 00:07:17,484
Now you know its danger, its grade of fight and what grows there, and
you may Travel there in a later season.

104
00:07:18,404 --> 00:07:20,999
Travel, one Food and the whole season.

105
00:07:21,069 --> 00:07:23,781
The whole party moves to a face-up tile next to it.

106
00:07:23,851 --> 00:07:30,962
Draw a Fortune card against the tile's danger number: on that number
or less, a patrol finds you and you fight as an ambush.

107
00:07:31,032 --> 00:07:35,287
A Guide makes the draw three better; Lao clothes or a travel pass, two
better.

108
00:07:35,357 --> 00:07:39,137
You gather the tile's forage on the way, and the season ends when you
arrive.

109
00:07:40,057 --> 00:07:41,305
Forage is free.

110
00:07:41,375 --> 00:07:44,493
Gain the Food shown on the tile for this season, plus one.

111
00:07:44,563 --> 00:07:48,981
Draw a Fortune card: on one to three you are spotted, and you fight as
an ambush.

112
00:07:49,901 --> 00:07:52,078
Rest or nurse, also free.

113
00:07:52,148 --> 00:07:55,080
Rest heals one wound, one more at a finished camp.

114
00:07:55,150 --> 00:08:02,169
Or nurse a sick villager: with medicine in the party the fever breaks
on a Fortune card of six or more, otherwise on eleven or more.

115
00:08:02,239 --> 00:08:06,866
With Kong on side B in the party, or Lee or Pa nursing, it always
breaks.

116
00:08:07,786 --> 00:08:10,277
Build a camp, one Food per action.

117
00:08:10,347 --> 00:08:12,896
Two actions finish a hidden camp on the tile.

118
00:08:12,966 --> 00:08:17,523
It makes the Winter Toll one better and resting heal one more, for as
long as you stay.

119
00:08:17,593 --> 00:08:24,170
Powers, playing a card from your hand, and giving an item to someone
else are actions too, unless the card says they are free.

120
00:08:25,090 --> 00:08:27,499
When the party cannot move, there is still work.

121
00:08:27,569 --> 00:08:31,953
Lay an ambush, once at each place, and the next fight there the party
fires first.

122
00:08:32,023 --> 00:08:34,699
Trade an item for three Food where people live.

123
00:08:34,769 --> 00:08:37,120
Share a meal: two Food for one Hope.

124
00:08:37,190 --> 00:08:43,721
Or seek help, once a season, and draw a Stranger card: a trader, a
deserter, a shaman, lost children.

125
00:08:43,791 --> 00:08:46,979
Each is a choice of two, and the party decides together.

126
00:08:47,899 --> 00:08:49,345
A word on carrying.

127
00:08:49,415 --> 00:08:53,995
Each villager has two hands, one body, one head and three pack slots.

128
00:08:54,065 --> 00:08:57,485
A rifle or a bow takes both hands; a knife takes one.

129
00:08:57,555 --> 00:09:02,089
Animals, boats and food caches belong to the whole party and take no
slot.

130
00:09:02,159 --> 00:09:07,157
When someone has too much, hand an item to someone with room, or leave
it in a cache on the tile.

131
00:09:11,277 --> 00:09:14,522
Back to the Fortune deck, because everything else runs on it.

132
00:09:14,592 --> 00:09:17,873
Twenty cards, one to twenty, shuffled face down.

133
00:09:17,943 --> 00:09:24,427
Whenever a rule asks for a draw, turn the top card, read the number
against the rule, and put the card on the discard.

134
00:09:24,497 --> 00:09:27,487
When the deck runs out, shuffle the discard and go on.

135
00:09:27,557 --> 00:09:35,563
Because every number comes out once before any comes again, a run of bad cards
means better ones are coming, and a table that counts can feel the deck turning.

136
00:09:35,633 --> 00:09:38,878
Each card also carries a Hmong saying for the moment.

137
00:09:42,998 --> 00:09:43,747
Fights.

138
00:09:43,817 --> 00:09:51,590
A fight happens when you draw a Danger or patrol card, when a forager
is spotted, when you are found travelling, at a key, and at the river.

139
00:09:51,660 --> 00:09:57,193
A fight has three steps: read the soldiers' number, clash up to three
times, and count the cost.

140
00:09:57,263 --> 00:09:59,429
There is nothing to add or multiply.

141
00:10:00,349 --> 00:10:02,596
Step one: read the soldiers' number.

142
00:10:02,666 --> 00:10:07,804
The soldiers have a single number, and it is their attack, their
defence and their hit points all at once.

143
00:10:07,874 --> 00:10:09,343
Find it on the Patrol table.

144
00:10:09,413 --> 00:10:15,003
The row is the grade of the fight: Easy, Medium, Hard, Deadly, or the
River Patrol.

145
00:10:15,073 --> 00:10:17,251
The column is how many of you are living.

146
00:10:17,321 --> 00:10:24,920
The block is the year: 1975 and 76, or 1977 onward, when the hunt
doubles.

147
00:10:24,990 --> 00:10:30,151
A party of four meeting a Hard patrol in 1977 faces fourteen.

148
00:10:31,071 --> 00:10:37,985
Your side adds together the HP, ATK and DEF of every living villager,
their items, and any cards played for this fight.

149
00:10:38,055 --> 00:10:41,150
Lay the fight tracker between you and write the numbers in.

150
00:10:42,070 --> 00:10:44,932
Step two: clash, up to three times.

151
00:10:45,002 --> 00:10:47,772
Each clash, first draw a Fortune card.

152
00:10:47,842 --> 00:10:52,190
On one to four the soldiers' aim is true: plus two attack for them
this clash.

153
00:10:52,260 --> 00:10:56,039
On seventeen to twenty the villagers find their mark: plus two for
you.

154
00:10:56,109 --> 00:10:58,043
Then both sides strike at once.

155
00:10:58,113 --> 00:11:00,487
You deal your ATK minus the soldiers' number.

156
00:11:00,557 --> 00:11:05,405
They deal their number minus your DEF, and always at least one,
because gunfire gets through.

157
00:11:05,475 --> 00:11:09,115
The party chooses who takes the wounds, and Armor stops them first.

158
00:11:10,035 --> 00:11:11,597
Here is a fight in the app.

159
00:11:11,667 --> 00:11:14,924
The soldiers fall when the damage you have dealt reaches their number.

160
00:11:14,994 --> 00:11:20,259
After three clashes, if they still stand, the party breaks away with
its wounds and nothing gained.

161
00:11:20,329 --> 00:11:23,911
A fallen villager's ATK and DEF leave the party at once.

162
00:11:23,981 --> 00:11:29,444
Draw a Fortune card for them: on one to ten they were killed, on
eleven to twenty they were taken prisoner.

163
00:11:29,514 --> 00:11:31,041
Either way they leave the game.

164
00:11:31,961 --> 00:11:33,709
A few things change a fight.

165
00:11:33,779 --> 00:11:37,837
In an ambush the soldiers fire first: you deal nothing in the first
clash.

166
00:11:37,907 --> 00:11:40,873
If you laid an ambush yourself, it is the other way round.

167
00:11:40,943 --> 00:11:46,836
An escape card, like a Hidden Path or Fog in the Valley, lets you slip
away with no fight at all.

168
00:11:46,906 --> 00:11:51,928
After the first or second clash you may break away: drop one item per
villager and take no hit.

169
00:11:51,998 --> 00:11:57,437
An Easy fight is village militia, and you may hand over two Food or a
money item instead of fighting.

170
00:11:57,507 --> 00:12:02,355
And a loud weapon leaves an Alarm token: the next fight there this
season is one row harder.

171
00:12:03,275 --> 00:12:05,174
Step three: count the cost.

172
00:12:05,244 --> 00:12:14,422
Win, and the party searches this place in safety: one card for an Easy fight,
two for Medium, three for Hard, skipping Danger, Nothing and key cards.

173
00:12:14,492 --> 00:12:17,238
The damage a survivor took becomes wounds.

174
00:12:17,308 --> 00:12:19,578
A fight you only survived gives nothing.

175
00:12:23,698 --> 00:12:27,733
The way out is a story cloth of nine squares, laid out three by three.

176
00:12:27,803 --> 00:12:34,554
Story cloths were first stitched in the Thai refugee camps by families
who had made this crossing, to record the war and the flight.

177
00:12:34,624 --> 00:12:37,336
Each square shows one stage of the escape.

178
00:12:37,406 --> 00:12:41,464
When a square is recovered, read its story aloud from the Companion.

179
00:12:41,534 --> 00:12:44,013
You need all nine, whatever the size of your party.

180
00:12:44,933 --> 00:12:54,134
The squares you did not start with are won with keys hidden in the search decks:
a letter from Nong Khai, signal fires on the ridge, a patrol timetable, a
fisherman's signal.

181
00:12:54,204 --> 00:12:57,020
Keys are scarce near home and plentiful near the river.

182
00:12:57,090 --> 00:13:02,565
Each key you win recovers the next missing square, and the living
villager carrying the fewest squares takes it.

183
00:13:03,485 --> 00:13:05,024
No square comes free.

184
00:13:05,094 --> 00:13:14,492
Each key names what stands between you and it, and the fight is always one step
harder than the place: Easy becomes Medium, Medium becomes Hard, Hard becomes
Deadly.

185
00:13:14,562 --> 00:13:16,194
A Guarded key is a fight.

186
00:13:16,264 --> 00:13:21,785
A Price key is paid with silver, baht, coins or two Food, or taken by
force.

187
00:13:21,855 --> 00:13:25,785
A key On the Fallen is taken now, and then his comrades ambush you.

188
00:13:25,855 --> 00:13:30,006
A Mined key costs everyone a Fortune draw, with wounds on one to four.

189
00:13:30,076 --> 00:13:34,181
Wait for Dark costs a Food each, and a patrol finds you on one to
eight.

190
00:13:34,251 --> 00:13:39,760
Or leave the key for now: put it at the bottom of the deck with a
Guard token on the tile, and come back for it.

191
00:13:40,680 --> 00:13:50,613
If a villager carrying squares is killed by soldiers or taken prisoner, their
squares lie where they fell: shuffle each into the top three cards of that
place's deck, to be won again.

192
00:13:50,683 --> 00:13:55,832
A villager who dies among the family, of hunger, sickness or the cold,
hands their squares on.

193
00:13:55,902 --> 00:14:06,137
And clues help you along the way: a Guide makes every travel draw three better,
a Trail Map reveals the next row, and a Safe Crossing Place or a Boatman stays
with its tile for the crossing.

194
00:14:10,257 --> 00:14:10,971
Winter.

195
00:14:11,041 --> 00:14:15,076
Every fourth season, at the end of the season, everyone eats one Food.

196
00:14:15,146 --> 00:14:21,654
Each Food you are short is a wound to someone who has not gone hungry
yet, and that person stays hungry until the next meal.

197
00:14:21,724 --> 00:14:24,749
Each Spring, everyone who ate heals one wound.

198
00:14:25,669 --> 00:14:26,755
Then the Toll.

199
00:14:26,825 --> 00:14:28,607
The cold gets worse every year.

200
00:14:28,677 --> 00:14:56,466
Every villager draws a Fortune card and falls sick on five or less, adjusted:
plus one for a child, an elder, the wounded or the already sick; plus one for
each Food short this year; plus the cold of the year, from zero in 1975 to two
in 1978 and 79; worse at low Hope and better at high Hope; one better with a
healer or a finished camp; and better for anyone holding a blanket, a poncho, a
mosquito net or quinine.

201
00:14:56,536 --> 00:14:59,747
A villager who is already sick and fails the Toll dies.

202
00:15:00,667 --> 00:15:03,924
Sick villagers act once a season instead of twice.

203
00:15:03,994 --> 00:15:10,444
They must be nursed each season, or at the end of it they draw for
fever, and die on a Fortune card of one to five.

204
00:15:10,514 --> 00:15:11,530
Nurse them early.

205
00:15:12,450 --> 00:15:15,231
Hope runs from zero to six and starts at three.

206
00:15:15,301 --> 00:15:19,127
Each death costs one Hope, unless a funeral is held.

207
00:15:19,197 --> 00:15:20,898
A hungry Winter costs one.

208
00:15:20,968 --> 00:15:25,131
Dilemmas and strangers raise or lower it, and sharing a meal raises
it.

209
00:15:25,201 --> 00:15:29,096
At Hope zero everyone has one action less and the Toll is two worse.

210
00:15:29,166 --> 00:15:31,889
At Hope five or six the Toll is one better.

211
00:15:31,959 --> 00:15:34,531
And at the river, Hope buys a second chance.

212
00:15:35,451 --> 00:15:37,942
After the Toll, the families hold a council.

213
00:15:38,012 --> 00:15:40,584
Draw two Law cards the party has not adopted.

214
00:15:40,654 --> 00:15:43,435
The party may adopt one and shuffles the other back.

215
00:15:43,505 --> 00:15:49,954
Council of Elders, Travel by Night, Proper Funerals, Everyone Nurses
the Sick, Strict Rations, Travel Light.

216
00:15:50,024 --> 00:15:53,281
Laws cannot be undone, and every one has a cost.

217
00:15:53,351 --> 00:15:55,691
Then the time marker moves to the next Spring.

218
00:15:59,811 --> 00:16:00,607
The river.

219
00:16:00,677 --> 00:16:06,023
With all nine squares on the cloth, the party may Cross as an action
from any river place.

220
00:16:06,093 --> 00:16:11,556
A Safe Crossing Place on that tile helps every check, and a Boatman
there sells seats for silver.

221
00:16:11,626 --> 00:16:16,369
The crossing has three parts: the River Patrol on the bank, the boats
and rafts, and the water.

222
00:16:17,289 --> 00:16:22,589
First, the River Patrol: Lao and Vietnamese soldiers with a machine
gun and a boat.

223
00:16:22,659 --> 00:16:27,135
Read the River Patrol row of the Patrol table; it counts at most five
people.

224
00:16:27,205 --> 00:16:29,986
Escape cards and ambushes do not apply here.

225
00:16:30,056 --> 00:16:31,665
Fight up to three clashes.

226
00:16:31,735 --> 00:16:33,889
Beat them and you reach the water unseen.

227
00:16:33,959 --> 00:16:41,070
If they still stand, the party breaks for the water under fire: the
Boatman will not come, but a canoe you found can still be launched.

228
00:16:41,990 --> 00:16:44,074
Second, boats and rafts.

229
00:16:44,144 --> 00:16:45,904
A dugout canoe carries two.

230
00:16:45,974 --> 00:16:50,426
With a Boatman, each money item buys one seat, and the boat takes four
a trip.

231
00:16:50,496 --> 00:16:56,145
Everyone else goes on a raft: free with raft poles or driftwood,
otherwise give up any two items.

232
00:16:56,215 --> 00:17:00,320
With no raft, they swim, and most highland villagers could not swim.

233
00:17:00,390 --> 00:17:02,335
Only Pao and Sheng can.

234
00:17:03,255 --> 00:17:04,585
Third, the water.

235
00:17:04,655 --> 00:17:09,444
Each person, children and the sick first, walks the Mekong lane with
up to three draws.

236
00:17:09,514 --> 00:17:14,977
Down to the water: on three or less they are hit, and on a one they
are killed at the water's edge.

237
00:17:15,047 --> 00:17:19,755
The current: draw a River card, read it aloud, then draw a Fortune
card.

238
00:17:19,825 --> 00:17:33,125
Swept away on thirteen or less, plus four in the monsoon, plus two for a child,
elder, sick or wounded person; six better in a boat, three better on a raft or
at a safe crossing place, and better with floats.

239
00:17:34,045 --> 00:17:43,177
Anyone the current takes draws again: drowned on twelve or less, worse for a
non-swimmer without a float, better if someone is already on the Thai bank to
throw a line.

240
00:17:43,247 --> 00:17:45,633
Above it, they crawl out on the Thai bank.

241
00:17:45,703 --> 00:17:51,038
If the river takes someone, you may spend one Hope to draw that check
again, once per person.

242
00:17:51,108 --> 00:17:54,771
A family that has held on to its spirit has a better chance at the
end.

243
00:17:58,891 --> 00:18:08,638
The game ends the moment someone reaches the Thai bank and no one is left in the
water, when the last villager dies or is taken, or at the end of Winter 1979.

244
00:18:08,708 --> 00:18:10,421
The ending is part of the game.

245
00:18:10,491 --> 00:18:11,565
Do not skip it.

246
00:18:12,485 --> 00:18:19,956
Read Ending A, Across the Mekong, if anyone crossed, or Ending B, The
ones who stayed, if no one did.

247
00:18:20,026 --> 00:18:22,842
Say aloud the names of those who did not reach the river.

248
00:18:22,912 --> 00:18:29,037
Shuffle the Voice cards of that ending, draw one and read it: each is
built from the recollection of a real person.

249
00:18:29,107 --> 00:18:36,578
Then, for every villager, find what became of them in the Endings booklet: their
name and a number, from one, crossed the Mekong, to ten.

250
00:18:36,648 --> 00:18:39,719
Each player names one thing their villager carried the whole way.

251
00:18:39,789 --> 00:18:41,351
And read the dedication.

252
00:18:45,471 --> 00:18:50,156
Let's play a season together, in the app, with Chai, Mai, Chao and
Blong.

253
00:18:50,226 --> 00:18:53,622
It is Spring 1975 in the Village Ruins.

254
00:18:53,692 --> 00:18:57,820
Food is twelve, Hope is three, and four squares of the cloth are sewn.

255
00:18:58,740 --> 00:19:00,499
The Season card comes first.

256
00:19:00,569 --> 00:19:04,233
We draw it and resolve it, and then the villagers act, Chai first.

257
00:19:05,153 --> 00:19:09,130
Chai searches the village: one Food, and the top card of the village
deck.

258
00:19:09,200 --> 00:19:10,855
The item goes to the family.

259
00:19:11,775 --> 00:19:13,070
Chai searches again.

260
00:19:13,140 --> 00:19:18,127
This is the second search here, so first a Fortune card: on a one,
soldiers would come.

261
00:19:18,197 --> 00:19:21,036
We are lucky, and Chai draws another card from the deck.

262
00:19:21,106 --> 00:19:24,107
His two actions are spent, so play passes to Mai.

263
00:19:25,027 --> 00:19:26,299
Mai is a farmer.

264
00:19:26,369 --> 00:19:33,329
She forages: the village gives its spring Food plus one, for free, and
her Fortune card is above three, so no one spots her.

265
00:19:34,249 --> 00:19:39,619
With her second action Mai scouts: one Food, and one of the hidden
places in the hills turns face up.

266
00:19:39,689 --> 00:19:42,110
Now the party knows where it can go next season.

267
00:19:43,030 --> 00:19:45,021
Chao and Blong finish the season.

268
00:19:45,091 --> 00:19:48,581
Chao searches once more, and Blong, the elder, rests.

269
00:19:48,651 --> 00:19:56,145
When the last villager is done, the season ends: no one is sick, it is
not Winter, so the time marker simply moves to Summer.

270
00:19:57,065 --> 00:19:59,173
Summer 1975.

271
00:19:59,243 --> 00:20:04,926
A new Season card, and then, before anyone acts, the family travels to
the airstrip Mai scouted.

272
00:20:04,996 --> 00:20:17,135
Travel normally costs one Food and a Fortune card against the place's danger
number, but Blong, the elder, uses his power, The Old Road: no danger draw this
time, and one more Food gathered on the way.

273
00:20:17,205 --> 00:20:19,196
The season ends when they arrive.

274
00:20:19,266 --> 00:20:23,185
Next season the search begins again, in a new place, with new cards.

275
00:20:23,255 --> 00:20:28,010
That is the rhythm of Chao Fa: look, decide, move, and keep the family
fed.

276
00:20:32,130 --> 00:20:33,889
A ladder of first games.

277
00:20:33,959 --> 00:20:41,059
Start with The First Winter, the printed first game, or the app's
Learn to play, with Chai, Mai, Chao and Blong.

278
00:20:41,129 --> 00:20:44,653
Then the same four on the Short Trail, making your own decisions.

279
00:20:44,723 --> 00:20:47,620
Then the full Trail with a party of four or five.

280
00:20:47,690 --> 00:20:53,873
After that, the villagers with the hardest powers, a setup card, side
B, and the Late Crossing scenario.

281
00:20:54,793 --> 00:20:57,435
Three golden rules when the table is unsure.

282
00:20:57,505 --> 00:20:59,252
A card beats the rulebook.

283
00:20:59,322 --> 00:21:01,813
A specific rule beats a general one.

284
00:21:01,883 --> 00:21:06,591
And when the table cannot agree, the elders decide: the player of the
oldest villager.

285
00:21:07,511 --> 00:21:12,277
The rulebook, the print-and-play kit and the free app are at the
address on screen.

286
00:21:12,347 --> 00:21:22,965
Chao Fa is dedicated to all the men and women who served in the Vietnam War, to
the Hmong who served and were killed, to those who died in the jungles of Laos
and those who are still there.

287
00:21:23,035 --> 00:21:25,398
Thank you for watching, and good luck on the trail.
